IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dog-act-domain`
IMPORT daydate

-- =============================================================================
-- Dog Act 1976 (Western Australia) -- Registration
--
-- Isomorphic encoding of Part III ("Registration and identification"),
-- Division 1 ("Registration"), ss 14, 15, 16, 16AA, 16A, 17A, 17, 18, 19, 20,
-- as at the compilation dated 28 Nov 2024 [version 08-b0-00], re-verified
-- current 2026-09-09. Source: lines 504-640 of mrdoc_47983.txt
-- (western-australia/dog-act-1976 source bundle).
--
-- This is a sibling encoding to dog-act-1976.l4 (Part VI Divisions 1-2) in
-- this same directory; it imports the shared s. 3 domain module
-- (dog-act-domain.l4) for the DogProfile ("dangerous dog") test and the
-- Penalty record shape only -- this Division's own actors (a registered
-- owner, a registration officer, a local government, the State
-- Administrative Tribunal, a Justice of the Peace) and facts are not shared
-- with Part VI's dangerous-dog material, so no LiableParty/AttackFacts value
-- from that module is read here. `IMPORT daydate` is added locally (beyond
-- the two imports every sibling file carries) because s. 15(2)(c)/(3A)/(6)
-- turn on real calendar dates ("the next 31 October", "after 31 May and
-- before 1 November") that this file computes rather than fact-supplies.
--
-- SCOPED OUT (cited at their site, never expanded): s. 8(1) ("assistance
-- dog"), s. 9 and s. 10(2) ("ordinarily kept"/deemed-ordinarily-kept), s. 21
-- and s. 22 (microchipping requirement and "the relevant day"), s. 31, 32,
-- 33A (seizure of unclaimed dogs generally), s. 33K(2)(c) (a Division 2
-- notification route, encoded in dog-act-1976.l4), s. 40(1) (a general
-- provision this section's seizure order displaces), s. 46A(2) (a
-- dog-ownership-ban order made under a Part outside this line range) --
-- every one of these is a fact-supplied BOOLEAN at its site, cited with
-- @ref, never expanded. The State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 ss
-- 46-48 (the proceeding-ended events s. 17(5) reaches) is likewise
-- fact-supplied, as an external Act.
--
-- No PARTY/MUST/WITHIN regulative rule appears for most of this Division:
-- almost every duty here is undated ("is to", "forthwith", "as soon as is
-- practicable", "the time fixed for the making of the application" -- fixed
-- by SAT procedure, not stated here) rather than carrying the Act's own
-- numeric deadline. The one exception is s. 16A(1)'s explicit "within 28
-- days" -- that gets a real regulative rule below, alongside the BOOLEAN
-- offence/Penalty pair the corpus's house style also gives every provision
-- that states a Penalty inline.
-- =============================================================================

§ `Shared penalty presets for this module`

-- The recurring flat $5,000-fine, no-imprisonment shape: ss 16A(1), 20(2).
`flat $5,000 fine penalty (ss 16A(1), 20(2))` MEANS
    Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

§ `Part III, Division 1 -- Registration`
§§ `14. Register of dogs`

-- s 14 is purely administrative machinery: a local government keeps a
-- register (1), in a form of its own choosing (2), recording the
-- prescribed particulars for each dog (3), and may correct errors or
-- omissions in it (4). No downstream rule in this Division tests a fact
-- about the register's existence, form, or correction as such -- s 14 is
-- read from, at s 16(2) and s 16(4), as the place particulars get entered
-- and notified, and those obligations are encoded at their own sites below.
-- Recorded here as inert prose rather than a force-fit predicate.

§§ `15. Registration periods and fees`

-- (1) -- the registration fee itself "shall be such amount as is prescribed
-- by regulation": a pure delegation to regulation, with no fact this
-- encoding computes. Every function below that needs a fee amount takes
-- "the fee that would otherwise be payable" as a fact-supplied NUMBER.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 15(2)(c), (3A) -- "until the next 31 October"
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next 31 October on or after` d MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH d AT MOST 10
    THEN YMD (DATE_YEAR d) 10 31
    ELSE YMD (DATE_YEAR d PLUS 1) 10 31

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 15(2)(c)
GIVEN `the date the registration took effect` IS A DATE, `the date being tested` IS A DATE, `the registration was cancelled sooner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a standard-period, non-dangerous dog's registration has effect on the date being tested (s 15(2)(c))` `the date the registration took effect` `the date being tested` `the registration was cancelled sooner` MEANS
        (NOT `the registration was cancelled sooner`)
    AND Day `the date being tested` AT MOST Day (`the next 31 October on or after` `the date the registration took effect`)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 15(3A)
GIVEN `the date the registration took effect` IS A DATE, `the date being tested` IS A DATE, `the registration was cancelled sooner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a dangerous dog's registration has effect on the date being tested (s 15(3A))` `the date the registration took effect` `the date being tested` `the registration was cancelled sooner` MEANS
        (NOT `the registration was cancelled sooner`)
    AND Day `the date being tested` AT MOST Day (`the next 31 October on or after` `the date the registration took effect`)

-- (2)(a)-(b): the two remaining s 15(2) terms turn on facts this file
-- cannot compute -- the length of "such extended period as is prescribed"
-- (s 15(3)(b), itself a regulation) and the date of the dog's death -- so
-- they stay fact-supplied booleans rather than derived dates.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 15(2)(a)-(b)
GIVEN `registration is for an extended period, and 31 October in the final year of that period has not yet passed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `registration is for the dog's lifetime, and the dog has not died` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the registration was cancelled sooner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an extended-period or lifetime non-dangerous dog's registration has effect (s 15(2)(a)-(b))` `registration is for an extended period, and 31 October in the final year of that period has not yet passed` `registration is for the dog's lifetime, and the dog has not died` `the registration was cancelled sooner` MEANS
        (NOT `the registration was cancelled sooner`)
    AND (   `registration is for an extended period, and 31 October in the final year of that period has not yet passed`
         OR `registration is for the dog's lifetime, and the dog has not died`)

-- (3), (4A), (4B) -- regulations may set concessional rates for six listed
-- classes of case (3), and a local government may separately discount or
-- waive a fee for any dog or class of dogs (4A), except that neither power
-- reaches a dangerous dog (4B). All three are administrative rate-setting
-- powers, not facts a downstream rule tests -- recorded as inert prose.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 15(4)
GIVEN `the dog is an assistance dog as defined in s 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the dog is kept for the purposes of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dog is exempt from a registration fee (s 15(4))` `the dog is an assistance dog as defined in s 8(1)` `the dog is kept for the purposes of the Crown` MEANS
    `the dog is an assistance dog as defined in s 8(1)` OR `the dog is kept for the purposes of the Crown`
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 8(1) "assistance dog" -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 15(5)
GIVEN `the fee that would otherwise be payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the registration fee for a droving or stock-tending dog (s 15(5))` `the fee that would otherwise be payable` MEANS
    `the fee that would otherwise be payable` DIVIDED BY 4

-- AMBIGUITY (F-DOG-ACT-P3-FEE-STACKING): ss 15(5) and 15(6) both discount
-- "the fee that would otherwise be payable", and a dog can meet both limbs
-- at once (a stock-tending dog on its first registration, taking effect
-- between 31 May and 1 November). The Act does not say whether the two
-- reductions stack (and if so, in which order), or whether only the more
-- specific provision applies. Taken reading: each function below is a pure
-- function of an "otherwise payable" fee supplied by the caller: this
-- encoding does not itself compose s 15(5) and s 15(6), leaving any
-- stacking question to whichever rule calls both. Rejected: silently
-- picking one order (e.g. quarter-then-half = one-eighth) as if the
-- statute settled it.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 15(6)
GIVEN `the date the first registration takes effect` IS A DATE, `the first registration is to have effect until 31 October in that year (a standard, non-extended, non-lifetime registration)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fee that would otherwise be payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the registration fee for a dog's first registration (s 15(6))` `the date the first registration takes effect` `the first registration is to have effect until 31 October in that year (a standard, non-extended, non-lifetime registration)` `the fee that would otherwise be payable` MEANS
    IF (   DATE_MONTH `the date the first registration takes effect` GREATER THAN 5
       AND DATE_MONTH `the date the first registration takes effect` LESS THAN 11
       AND `the first registration is to have effect until 31 October in that year (a standard, non-extended, non-lifetime registration)`)
    THEN `the fee that would otherwise be payable` DIVIDED BY 2
    ELSE `the fee that would otherwise be payable`

§§ `16. Registration procedure`

DECLARE `S16(1) Application Facts` HAS
    `the dog is ordinarily kept in the district, or is deemed ordinarily kept there under s 9 or s 10(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 9, s. 10(2) -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `an application in the prescribed form, signed by or on behalf of the owner, was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application was accompanied by the prescribed fee, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application was delivered to the local government's office, or another place within the district appointed by the local government for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(1)
GIVEN f IS A `S16(1) Application Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dog may be registered by the local government (s 16(1))` f MEANS
        f's `the dog is ordinarily kept in the district, or is deemed ordinarily kept there under s 9 or s 10(2)`
    AND f's `an application in the prescribed form, signed by or on behalf of the owner, was delivered`
    AND f's `the application was accompanied by the prescribed fee, if any`
    AND f's `the application was delivered to the local government's office, or another place within the district appointed by the local government for the purpose`

DECLARE `S16 Application Form` HAS
    `provides the owner's name, residential address and contact details` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides the address of the premises where the dog will ordinarily be kept` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states that the dog will be effectively confined in or at those premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog is microchipped`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `if the dog is microchipped, provides the microchip database company's name`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `if the dog is microchipped, provides the microchip's unique identification number`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `states whether the dog is kept, or is to be kept, as a commercial security dog`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `states whether the owner is subject to an order under s 46A(2)`                            IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 46A(2) -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(1BA)
GIVEN f IS A `S16 Application Form`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application form satisfies s 16(1BA)'s content requirements` f MEANS
        f's `provides the owner's name, residential address and contact details`
    AND f's `provides the address of the premises where the dog will ordinarily be kept`
    AND f's `states that the dog will be effectively confined in or at those premises`
    AND (   (NOT f's `the dog is microchipped`)
         OR (   f's `if the dog is microchipped, provides the microchip database company's name`
             AND f's `if the dog is microchipped, provides the microchip's unique identification number`))
    AND f's `states whether the dog is kept, or is to be kept, as a commercial security dog`
    AND f's `states whether the owner is subject to an order under s 46A(2)`

-- (1BB) -- nothing prevents the prescribed form requiring additional
-- information: a permissive drafting note about the form's scope, not a
-- fact any rule here tests. Inert prose.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(1b)
GIVEN `the dog is ordinarily kept by a person under 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN, `the application was made by that person's parent or guardian, or another person who is 18 years of age or older` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application for a dog ordinarily kept by a minor complies with s 16(1b)` `the dog is ordinarily kept by a person under 18 years of age` `the application was made by that person's parent or guardian, or another person who is 18 years of age or older` MEANS
    (NOT `the dog is ordinarily kept by a person under 18 years of age`) OR `the application was made by that person's parent or guardian, or another person who is 18 years of age or older`

-- s 16(1b)'s further clause -- "any registration shall be in the name of
-- the applicant" -- is a recording instruction for how the s 14 register is
-- filled in once an application already complies with the test above, not
-- itself a further condition any downstream rule here tests. Inert prose.

DECLARE `S16(2) Outcome` IS ONE OF
    `effect the registration (s 16(2)(a))`
    `refuse the application and refund the fee (s 16(2)(b))`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(2)
GIVEN `the local government directs the registration officer to refuse the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `S16(2) Outcome`
`the registration officer's action on a duly-made application (s 16(2))` `the local government directs the registration officer to refuse the application` MEANS
    IF `the local government directs the registration officer to refuse the application`
    THEN `refuse the application and refund the fee (s 16(2)(b))`
    ELSE `effect the registration (s 16(2)(a))`

DECLARE `S16(3A) Ban Facts` HAS
    `a s 46A(2) order bans the person from owning or keeping a dog, and that order's period has not expired` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 46A(2) -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    `the dog is registered in that person's name in this local government's district` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(3A)(a)
GIVEN f IS A `S16(3A) Ban Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the registration officer must cancel the dog's registration (s 16(3A)(a))` f MEANS
        f's `a s 46A(2) order bans the person from owning or keeping a dog, and that order's period has not expired`
    AND f's `the dog is registered in that person's name in this local government's district`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(3A)(b)
GIVEN `a s 46A(2) order bans the person from owning or keeping a dog, and that order's period has not expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a registration officer must not effect or renew the dog's registration in that person's name (s 16(3A)(b))` `a s 46A(2) order bans the person from owning or keeping a dog, and that order's period has not expired` MEANS
    `a s 46A(2) order bans the person from owning or keeping a dog, and that order's period has not expired`
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 46A(2) -- scoped out, fact-supplied

DECLARE `S16(3) Grounds` HAS
    `the applicant, the owner, or the registered owner has been convicted, or has paid a modified penalty, within the previous 3 years for 2 or more offences against this Act, the Cat Act 2011 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog has been shown to the local government's satisfaction to be destructive, unduly mischievous, or to be suffering from a contagious or infectious disease` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the local government is not satisfied that the dog is, or will be, effectively confined in or at premises where the dog is, or will be, ordinarily kept` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog is required under s 21 or s 22 to be microchipped but is not microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 21, s. 22 -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(3)
GIVEN g IS A `S16(3) Grounds`, dog IS A DogProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`grounds exist for the local government to direct refusal or cancellation of registration (s 16(3))` g dog MEANS
        g's `the applicant, the owner, or the registered owner has been convicted, or has paid a modified penalty, within the previous 3 years for 2 or more offences against this Act, the Cat Act 2011 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002`
    OR  g's `the dog has been shown to the local government's satisfaction to be destructive, unduly mischievous, or to be suffering from a contagious or infectious disease`
    OR  g's `the local government is not satisfied that the dog is, or will be, effectively confined in or at premises where the dog is, or will be, ordinarily kept`
    OR  g's `the dog is required under s 21 or s 22 to be microchipped but is not microchipped`
    OR  `the dog is a dangerous dog` dog

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(3c)
GIVEN `it is proved to the registration officer's satisfaction that the dog has died or has been removed from the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the registration officer may cancel the registration (s 16(3c))` `it is proved to the registration officer's satisfaction that the dog has died or has been removed from the State` MEANS
    `it is proved to the registration officer's satisfaction that the dog has died or has been removed from the State`

DECLARE `S16(4) Notice` HAS
    `given forthwith upon the refusal, non-renewal or cancellation of the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanied by a statement in writing of the grounds upon which the local government's decision was made` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(4)
GIVEN n IS A `S16(4) Notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 16(4) notice satisfies its requirements` n MEANS
        n's `given forthwith upon the refusal, non-renewal or cancellation of the registration`
    AND n's `accompanied by a statement in writing of the grounds upon which the local government's decision was made`

-- (5) -- registration under this Act has effect throughout the State
-- notwithstanding removal to another district: a rule about the geographic
-- reach of an already-existing registration, not itself a fact any
-- downstream predicate here tests. Inert prose.

DECLARE `S16(6) Registration Delivery` HAS
    `the certificate delivered acknowledges the fee paid and specifies the registration number, the term of the registration period, and a description of the dog` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a registration tag of the prescribed kind was delivered`                                                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16(6)
GIVEN d IS A `S16(6) Registration Delivery`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 16(6) delivery satisfies its requirements` d MEANS
        d's `the certificate delivered acknowledges the fee paid and specifies the registration number, the term of the registration period, and a description of the dog`
    AND d's `a registration tag of the prescribed kind was delivered`

§§ `16AA. Owner's delegate`

DECLARE `S16AA Appointment` HAS
    `made in writing, given to the local government with which the dog is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the prescribed form`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the appointee has reached 18 years of age`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `terminated in writing by the registered owner or the appointed person`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person who made the appointment has ceased to be the registered owner of the dog` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16AA(1), (3)
GIVEN a IS A `S16AA Appointment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointment of an owner's delegate is validly made (s 16AA(1),(3))` a MEANS
        a's `made in writing, given to the local government with which the dog is registered`
    AND a's `in the prescribed form`
    AND a's `the appointee has reached 18 years of age`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16AA(4)-(5)
GIVEN a IS A `S16AA Appointment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointment of an owner's delegate remains in effect (s 16AA(4)-(5))` a MEANS
    NOT (   a's `terminated in writing by the registered owner or the appointed person`
         OR a's `the person who made the appointment has ceased to be the registered owner of the dog`)

-- (2) -- a local government may deal with the owner's delegate instead of
-- the owner "in the circumstances specified in this Act": a discretionary
-- administrative choice about who a local government transacts with, not a
-- further fact this encoding tests -- what matters downstream is only
-- whether the appointment is validly made and still in effect, both
-- already captured above. Inert prose.

§§ `16A. Change of ownership`

DECLARE RegistrationParty IS ONE OF
    `Registered Owner`
    `Local Government`
    `Registration Officer`

DECLARE RegistrationAction IS ONE OF
    `notify the local government of the new owner under s 16A(1)`

-- s 16A(1) applies only "[w]here the ownership of a dog, OTHER THAN A
-- DANGEROUS DOG, is transferred" -- a dangerous dog's change of ownership is
-- instead governed by s 33K(4)-(5A) (Part VI Division 2, already encoded in
-- dog-act-1976.l4). The PARTY/MUST/WITHIN template below models the 28-day
-- duty as such and is only meant to be invoked for a non-dangerous dog's
-- transfer; the offence predicate immediately below it is where that
-- precondition is actually tested and enforced, since it is the operative,
-- computed consequence this file asserts against.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16A(1)
`s 16A(1) notification duty -- change of ownership` MEANS
    PARTY `Registered Owner`
    MUST  `notify the local government of the new owner under s 16A(1)`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `Registered Owner`
          BECAUSE "the local government was not notified of the new owner's name and residential address within 28 days, as s 16A(1) requires"

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16A(1) Penalty
GIVEN `the registered owner failed to cause the local government to be notified, within 28 days of the transfer, of the new owner's name and residential address` IS A BOOLEAN, dog IS A DogProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16A(1) offence -- failing to notify a change of ownership within 28 days` `the registered owner failed to cause the local government to be notified, within 28 days of the transfer, of the new owner's name and residential address` dog MEANS
        (NOT `the dog is a dangerous dog` dog)
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16A(1) "other than a dangerous dog" -- s 16A(1)'s duty, and this offence, do not reach a dangerous dog; see s 33K(4)-(5A) instead
    AND `the registered owner failed to cause the local government to be notified, within 28 days of the transfer, of the new owner's name and residential address`

`s 16A(1) penalty` MEANS `flat $5,000 fine penalty (ss 16A(1), 20(2))`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16A(2)
GIVEN `the registered owner notified the change under s 16A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the registered owner notified the change under s 33K(2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN, `an application for registration was made by a person alleging to be the new owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government may record the change of ownership (s 16A(2))` `the registered owner notified the change under s 16A(1)` `the registered owner notified the change under s 33K(2)(c)` `an application for registration was made by a person alleging to be the new owner` MEANS
        `the registered owner notified the change under s 16A(1)`
    OR  `the registered owner notified the change under s 33K(2)(c)`
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 33K(2)(c) -- Division 2 material, encoded in dog-act-1976.l4 -- scoped out, fact-supplied
    OR  `an application for registration was made by a person alleging to be the new owner`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 16A(3)
GIVEN `a person is aggrieved by a local government decision relating to the ownership of a dog as recorded in a register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may apply to SAT for review of an ownership decision (s 16A(3))` `a person is aggrieved by a local government decision relating to the ownership of a dog as recorded in a register` MEANS
    `a person is aggrieved by a local government decision relating to the ownership of a dog as recorded in a register`

§§ `17A. If no application for registration made`

-- (1) -- defines "dog", for this section only, as a dog ordinarily kept (or
-- deemed ordinarily kept under s 9 or s 10(2), scoped out) in the district
-- for which no application for registration has been made. This gate is
-- folded directly into the fact-supplied grounds below rather than encoded
-- as a separate predicate: nothing downstream needs "is this an s 17A
-- dog" as a standalone fact once the grounds themselves are being tested.

DECLARE `S17A Grounds` HAS
    `the owner, or the registered owner, has been convicted, or has paid a modified penalty, within the previous 3 years for 2 or more offences against this Act, the Cat Act 2011 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog has been shown to the local government's satisfaction to be destructive, unduly mischievous, or suffering from a contagious or infectious disease` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the local government is not satisfied that the dog is, or will be, effectively confined in or at premises where the dog is, or will be, ordinarily kept` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog is required under s 21 or s 22 to be microchipped but is not microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 21, s. 22 -- scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 17A(2)
GIVEN g IS A `S17A Grounds`, dog IS A DogProfile
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`grounds exist for the local government to give a s 17A(2) notice that the dog cannot be registered` g dog MEANS
        g's `the owner, or the registered owner, has been convicted, or has paid a modified penalty, within the previous 3 years for 2 or more offences against this Act, the Cat Act 2011 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002`
    OR  g's `the dog has been shown to the local government's satisfaction to be destructive, unduly mischievous, or suffering from a contagious or infectious disease`
    OR  g's `the local government is not satisfied that the dog is, or will be, effectively confined in or at premises where the dog is, or will be, ordinarily kept`
    OR  g's `the dog is required under s 21 or s 22 to be microchipped but is not microchipped`
    OR  `the dog is a dangerous dog` dog

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 17A(3)
GIVEN `the notice informs the owner of the s 17(1) right to apply for review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 17A(2) notice satisfies s 17A(3)'s content requirement` `the notice informs the owner of the s 17(1) right to apply for review` MEANS
    `the notice informs the owner of the s 17(1) right to apply for review`

§§ `17. Refusal or cancellation of registration`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 17(1)
GIVEN `the local government refused to effect or renew the registration of the dog` IS A BOOLEAN, `the local government cancelled a registration of the dog` IS A BOOLEAN, `the local government gave a written notice under s 17A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicant, registered owner or owner may apply to SAT for review (s 17(1))` `the local government refused to effect or renew the registration of the dog` `the local government cancelled a registration of the dog` `the local government gave a written notice under s 17A(2)` MEANS
        `the local government refused to effect or renew the registration of the dog`
    OR  `the local government cancelled a registration of the dog`
    OR  `the local government gave a written notice under s 17A(2)`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 17(3)
GIVEN `SAT affirms the decision of the local government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`SAT must order seizure, detention and destruction of the dog (s 17(3))` `SAT affirms the decision of the local government` MEANS
    `SAT affirms the decision of the local government`
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 40(1) -- displaced, scoped out

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 17(3a)
GIVEN `SAT is satisfied that the dog will be kept without the likelihood of any contravention of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`SAT may cancel a suspended s 17(3) order (s 17(3a))` `SAT is satisfied that the dog will be kept without the likelihood of any contravention of this Act` MEANS
    `SAT is satisfied that the dog will be kept without the likelihood of any contravention of this Act`
-- SAT's separate power, at the same subsection, to suspend the s 17(3)
-- order in the first place and impose conditions on the suspension is a
-- pure, uncriteria'd discretion -- the text states no test for exercising
-- it, only for later cancelling the suspension (captured above). Inert
-- prose for the suspension power itself.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 17(4)
GIVEN `an application for review under s 17(1) was not made within the time fixed for making the application` IS A BOOLEAN, `a Justice of the Peace is satisfied that the applicant, registered owner or owner was given proper notice of the reason for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN, `a Justice of the Peace is satisfied that no application for review of the decision was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Justice of the Peace may order the seizure of the dog under s 17(4)` `an application for review under s 17(1) was not made within the time fixed for making the application` `a Justice of the Peace is satisfied that the applicant, registered owner or owner was given proper notice of the reason for the decision` `a Justice of the Peace is satisfied that no application for review of the decision was made` MEANS
        `an application for review under s 17(1) was not made within the time fixed for making the application`
    AND `a Justice of the Peace is satisfied that the applicant, registered owner or owner was given proper notice of the reason for the decision`
    AND `a Justice of the Peace is satisfied that no application for review of the decision was made`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 17(5)
GIVEN `an application for review was made under s 17(1) but the proceeding on it was withdrawn, dismissed or struck out under s 46, 47 or 48 of the State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Justice of the Peace may order the seizure of the dog under s 17(5)` `an application for review was made under s 17(1) but the proceeding on it was withdrawn, dismissed or struck out under s 46, 47 or 48 of the State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004` MEANS
    `an application for review was made under s 17(1) but the proceeding on it was withdrawn, dismissed or struck out under s 46, 47 or 48 of the State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004`
        -- @ref State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) ss. 46-48 -- external Act, scoped out, fact-supplied

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 17(6)
GIVEN `a seizure order was made under s 17(4) or s 17(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government may seize, detain, destroy or dispose of the dog under s 17(6)` `a seizure order was made under s 17(4) or s 17(5)` MEANS
    `a seizure order was made under s 17(4) or s 17(5)`
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss. 31, 32, 33A -- scoped out, fact-supplied

§§ `18. Registration tags`

DECLARE `Registration Tag` HAS
    `made of a durable material`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `is of the colour specified by the Minister under s 18(2) for the relevant registration period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains the prescribed particulars`                              IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 18(1)
GIVEN t IS A `Registration Tag`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the registration tag complies with s 18(1)` t MEANS
        t's `made of a durable material`
    AND t's `is of the colour specified by the Minister under s 18(2) for the relevant registration period`
    AND t's `contains the prescribed particulars`

-- (2)-(3) -- the Minister's power to specify (and later amend or replace)
-- the colour of registration tags for a registration period, by order
-- published in the Gazette: administrative rule-making. The only
-- downstream fact this Division tests is whether a given tag IS of the
-- specified colour, already captured above. Inert prose.

§§ `19. Refund of fee on cancellation`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 19
GIVEN `the registration was for an extended period` IS A BOOLEAN, `the registration was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person who was the registered owner returned the registration tag to the local government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the registered owner is entitled to a refund under s 19` `the registration was for an extended period` `the registration was cancelled` `the person who was the registered owner returned the registration tag to the local government` MEANS
        `the registration was for an extended period`
    AND `the registration was cancelled`
    AND `the person who was the registered owner returned the registration tag to the local government`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 19
GIVEN `the registered owner is entitled to a refund under s 19` IS A BOOLEAN, `the refund amount as prescribed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount refundable under s 19` `the registered owner is entitled to a refund under s 19` `the refund amount as prescribed` MEANS
    IF `the registered owner is entitled to a refund under s 19` THEN `the refund amount as prescribed` ELSE 0

§§ `20. Offences relating to registration etc.`

DECLARE `S20(1) Conduct Facts` HAS
    `wilfully inserted or omitted, or permitted to be inserted or omitted, in an application for the grant or renewal of a registration, any matter or thing contrary to, or for the purpose of concealing, the truth (s 20(1)(a))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kept a dog wearing a registration tag issued in respect of another dog (s 20(1)(c)(ii))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kept a dog wearing a registration tag in respect of a registration which is cancelled (s 20(1)(c)(iii))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wrongfully removed or defaced a registration tag issued under this Act (s 20(1)(d))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made, used, purchased or had in his possession a counterfeit or false certificate of registration or registration tag, or anything apparently intended to resemble or pass for the same (s 20(1)(d))` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 20(1)
GIVEN f IS A `S20(1) Conduct Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) offence -- wilfully falsifying an application, misusing a registration tag, or counterfeiting registration documents` f MEANS
        f's `wilfully inserted or omitted, or permitted to be inserted or omitted, in an application for the grant or renewal of a registration, any matter or thing contrary to, or for the purpose of concealing, the truth (s 20(1)(a))`
    OR  f's `kept a dog wearing a registration tag issued in respect of another dog (s 20(1)(c)(ii))`
    OR  f's `kept a dog wearing a registration tag in respect of a registration which is cancelled (s 20(1)(c)(iii))`
    OR  f's `wrongfully removed or defaced a registration tag issued under this Act (s 20(1)(d))`
    OR  f's `made, used, purchased or had in his possession a counterfeit or false certificate of registration or registration tag, or anything apparently intended to resemble or pass for the same (s 20(1)(d))`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 20(1) Penalty
GIVEN dog IS A DogProfile
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 20(1) penalty` dog MEANS
    IF `the dog is a dangerous dog` dog
    THEN Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 10_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING
    ELSE Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000,  `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 20(2)
GIVEN `regulations provide that a prescribed tattoo may be accepted by a local government as proof that the dog has been sterilised` IS A BOOLEAN, `a person applied, or caused to be applied, the prescribed tattoo to an unsterilised dog` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) offence -- applying the prescribed sterilisation tattoo to an unsterilised dog` `regulations provide that a prescribed tattoo may be accepted by a local government as proof that the dog has been sterilised` `a person applied, or caused to be applied, the prescribed tattoo to an unsterilised dog` MEANS
        `regulations provide that a prescribed tattoo may be accepted by a local government as proof that the dog has been sterilised`
    AND `a person applied, or caused to be applied, the prescribed tattoo to an unsterilised dog`

`s 20(2) penalty` MEANS `flat $5,000 fine penalty (ss 16A(1), 20(2))`

